    <statement><p>Find the least common denominator (LCD) of the rational expressions:  
<me>\frac{6t+1}{16t^{2}+24t+9} \mbox{ and } \frac{2t+3}{16t^{2}-9}</me></p>
<p>LCD:  <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(4t-3\right)\mathopen{}\left(4t+3\right)^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The factors of the denominators are</p>
<p><m>16t^{2}+24t+9 = \left(4t+3\right)^{2}</m></p>
<p><m>16t^{2}-9= \left(4t+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(4t-3\right)</m></p>
<p>Hence, the LCD is <m>\left(4t-3\right)\mathopen{}\left(4t+3\right)^{2}</m>.</p>
</solution>
